From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] Tests - tighter assertions and missing cases of the
 series

Review of this series; tests only.

SSLSocketTest:
- test_SSLSocket_ClientHello_padding asserts the padded ClientHello is
  exactly 512 bytes (OpenSSL 1.0.1u pads the handshake message to
  0x200), not at least 512.
- getSupportedCipherSuites_connect: the non-export DHE suites from the
  AndroidOpenSSL client to the HarmonyJSSE server (libcore/0024) must
  now fail in the client with SSLHandshakeException "dh key too small"
  (OpenSSL's Logjam check against the 512-bit group); before, any
  exception counted as the expected failure.
- handshakeWrapped (session reuse tests) uses 30 s socket and future
  timeouts, so a stalled handshake fails the test instead of the run.
  test_SSLSocket_sessionReuse_onlyWhenResumed stays a guard test: it
  passes before and after cm-11 3f575a6.
- test_SSLSocket_SNI_ipLiteral_noReverseDns is renamed
  test_SSLSocket_SNI_wrappedIpLiteral_noReverseDns: it covers a wrapped
  socket only and passed before the SNI-by-default port too. New
  test_SSLSocket_SNI_inetAddress_noReverseDns: for a platform socket
  created with an InetAddress, the SNI helper returns null and does not
  resolve the peer's name (the handshake still does, for the session
  cache key, as in 4.4 and 6.0, so the helper is called directly).
- The ClientHello capture helper (upstream 0007cf6/b1fe85c) no longer
  races: the reading task closed the accepted socket itself, so the
  client could fail and cancel the reading future before call()
  returned, and get() threw CancellationException although the
  ClientHello had been read (seen on the single-vCPU emulator). The
  test thread now closes it after get(). A client that fails before
  sending a ClientHello is reported with its own exception: the
  IOException its startHandshake() ended with (swallowed as expected
  before) becomes the cause of the helper's exception, so a
  CancellationException never hides why nothing was captured. New
  test_SSLSocket_ClientHello_captureReportsEarlyClientFailure (a never
  connected socket; failed with CancellationException before).

SSLSocketFactoryTest.test_SSLSocketFactory_getDefault_isProviderClass:
getDefault() is the class named by ssl.SocketFactory.provider whenever
that class is loadable (libcore/0025 names the layer-D wrapper;
getDefault() falls back silently if it cannot create it).

URLConnectionTest.testSslFallback_socketWithoutScsvSupport: okhttp's
TLSv1 retry with a socket that does not list TLS_FALLBACK_SCSV as
supported (a delegating ScsvHidingSSLSocket around the platform socket)
goes out without it and connects (the c3f6560 branch that had no
runtime test). A HarmonyJSSE client factory cannot serve here: its
createSocket(Socket, host, port, autoClose) throws a
NullPointerException on 4.4 (SSLSocketWrapper initialises its transport
in the superclass constructor before the wrapped socket is set).

TrustManagerImplTest.testLearnedIntermediateCrossSignedPairTerminates:
the bare leaf and the chain ending in the cross-signed cycle must
terminate within 60 s and be either rejected or accepted with a trusted
chain from the leaf to the root (a valid path through I_R exists; the
4.4 walk rejects it, a backtracking builder may accept it). The worker
thread is shared by a runWithin helper.
